---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { gh, u } from '../lib/url';
import { shortDate } from '../lib/date';

// Dated milestones, taken from the repos' own status notes and commit history.
// Add new entries at the top.
const entries = [
  { date: '2026-10-09', title: 'The scorecard moves to 84', text: 'A new run of the Airframe scorecard: 84 out of 100, up from 72, and 10 of the 14 A+ checks now pass. Most of the gain came from fixes the architecture review asked for: an owner and a risk class on every values field, AGENTS.md on every component, and status conditions and reason codes on almost every XRD. That clears the M2 target of 75. The first run today said 82, because the tool had lost track of a folder rename; I fixed the tool and said so on the page.', href: u('scorecard/') },
  { date: '2026-10-05', title: 'A service catalog that grows with the company', text: "An essay on taking Hangar's catalog past Kubernetes: Lambda functions, Azure Functions and three cloud deploy targets, added across Glidepath, Airframe and Tower on October 3 and 4. Why an API is the right front door to the cloud, how architecture and security policy can live inside a Crossplane XR as code, and an honest note on what isn't built yet. Three new diagrams go with it.", href: u('architecture/catalog-that-grows/') },
  { date: '2026-10-03', title: 'Why Hangar runs its tests in Testkube', text: 'An essay on choosing Testkube: the proof of concept with a team of test engineers that sold me on it, how it works, why tests as Kubernetes resources fit an API-driven control plane, and what running the free tier taught me. Three new Testing diagrams go with it, and Testkube and TestWorkflow join the glossary.', href: u('architecture/why-testkube/') },
  { date: '2026-10-02', title: 'How Hangar started', text: 'A Field note on where Hangar came from: rebuilding my home lab while learning to build with AI, the five mockups that became my first Backstage plugin, how Radar shaped the look, and how Glidepath, Tower and Hangar got their names. With a second note, a shout-out to the diagram-design skill behind every diagram here.', href: u('notes/origin/') },
  { date: '2026-10-02', title: 'Hangar at a glance', text: 'The home page gets its own architecture diagram: one road from intent to production, with a reviewed commit as the only thing that crosses into a cluster. It plays through once, and every box opens the page behind it. Four more high-level views join it in the diagrams, all wearing the product marks.', href: u('diagrams/#overview') },
  { date: '2026-10-01', title: 'The parachute sentence, spelled out', text: 'Several pages and diagrams leaned on "the parachute sentence" without ever saying what it was. It is the one request Autopilot is built to pass: an agent asked to provision a new Python app named parachute, with four environments, a canary step and an env var. It is now quoted where it first appears, in the glossary, and in the diagrams that name it.', href: u('glossary/#parachute-sentence') },
  { date: '2026-09-30', title: 'Why a platform still needs a service catalog', text: 'An essay on why Airframe sits at the centre of Hangar: the difference between a catalog\'s menu and its inventory, why the contract matters more than the list once agents are reading it, build versus buy now that AI writes code, and the discovery-first plan I\'d bring to a platform team. Five new diagrams go with it.', href: u('architecture/why-airframe/') },
  { date: '2026-09-30', title: 'Field notes, and a shout-out to Radar', text: 'A new section for shorter posts. The first one is about Radar, the open source Kubernetes UI from Skyhook: the people behind it, and the Tekton and Argo Rollouts features I added while learning to build with AI.', href: u('notes/radar/') },
  { date: '2026-09-30', title: 'Building Airframe, part 1', text: 'The first of a series on building Airframe with Crossplane: the secret store I never got to prototype, what "ready" really means, three ways I emptied GitHub\'s API budget, and the day rendering nothing deleted two apps\' secrets. Four new diagrams go with it.', href: u('architecture/building-airframe/') },
  { date: '2026-09-29', title: 'The Airframe scorecard, over time', text: 'The scorecard gets its own page, with every committed run on one chart: 27 at the baseline, 41 after M0, and 72 now that M1 and M2 are closed, with 7 of the 14 A+ checks passing. The first run today said 58, because the tool was looking for things where they were first planned to live, not where they ended up. I fixed the tool and said so on the page.', href: u('scorecard/') },
  { date: '2026-09-28', title: 'Plain words, and honest labels', text: 'A glossary of the jargon, with a short explainer on the first mention of each term on every page, and a status on each product card, so Autopilot no longer looks as finished as Glidepath.', href: u('glossary/') },
  { date: '2026-09-28', title: 'An Architecture section', text: 'A home for pointed opinions, argued from what Hangar does and what it has cost. The first essay is about the bill for running this platform, and where Crossplane should stop.', href: u('architecture/') },
  { date: '2026-09-28', title: 'Zero to running, twice, for real', text: 'Two new services taken from nothing to production and recorded: gate-api in the terminal, checkin-api in Tower. Running the whole path end to end found four real platform bugs the unit tests had missed, three of them from the release-file split. All four are fixed.', href: u('run/') },
  { date: '2026-09-27', title: 'The stack, as decisions', text: 'Every tool in Hangar on one page, each with what I chose it over and why, and the same tools on the homepage in the order a change meets them.', href: u('stack/') },
  { date: '2026-09-27', title: 'An architecture review', text: 'A staff-architect review of the whole platform: a conditional approval, ten findings with evidence, and five gates before production. The biggest are prod\'s dependency on the dev cluster, identity on a personal GitHub account, and no restore plan.', href: u('review/') },
  { date: '2026-09-27', title: 'This site', text: 'Hangar gets a home on the web: the platform, its principles and its diagrams in one place, built from the same repo.' },
  { date: '2026-09-26', title: 'Autopilot, the sixth product', text: 'Design for running any AI agent workload, bounded and audited. The Clearance core, the AppSpec planner, nine Skyport agent definitions and six Preflight cases are built and tested; the AgentRun XRD is drafted. The Airframe scorecard lands with a committed baseline of 27 out of 100.', href: gh('hangar', 'docs/autopilot/README.md') },
  { date: '2026-09-23', title: 'Infisical operator retired on the prod cluster', text: 'All five apps and Glidepath itself migrated onto the new Airframe pin and External Secrets, phase by phase, with the plan and each phase recorded as it closed.' },
  { date: '2026-09-22', title: 'The prod cluster, rebuilt', text: 'The upper cluster is rebuilt from the Apron template instead of being patched in place.' },
  { date: '2026-09-21', title: 'Every app stack scaffolds its cicd.yaml', text: 'The last hand-authored step in onboarding goes away. The same week, docs across every repo get one table of contents and TechDocs wiring in Tower.', href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/adr/0017-cicd-yaml-scaffolded-not-hand-authored.md') },
  { date: '2026-09-17', title: 'SecretStore on Infisical, built', text: 'One secret store per app and cluster, shared across that app\'s environments, never across clusters.', href: gh('hangar', 'docs/service-catalog-design.md') },
  { date: '2026-09-07', title: 'The Hangar brand', text: 'The project is renamed Hangar, with the instrument-dial mark family: one gauge, one glyph per product, and the calm-cockpit colour rule.', href: gh('hangar', 'brand/README.md') },
  { date: '2026-09-05', title: 'A self-hosted transparency log', text: 'Rekor and Trillian join the self-hosted Fulcio, so image signatures get a real transparency-log timestamp.', href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/adr/0014-keyless-signing-two-trust-roots.md') },
  { date: '2026-08-24', title: 'Testkube, and reading the source', text: 'The documented multi-namespace mode turns out to be paid-only in the source. The shared-namespace design ships, with a Kyverno policy closing the gap RBAC cannot.', href: gh('glidepath', 'docs/admin/adr/0007-testkube-shared-namespace.md') },
  { date: '2026-08-16', title: 'Lower and upper environments become a real boundary', text: 'Built and verified live after a real bug: a separate AppProject, not just a separate folder.', href: gh('hangar', 'docs/gitops-strategy.md') },
  { date: '2026-08-13', title: 'AI triage in the control plane', text: 'A Composition Function watches Argo Rollouts and dispatches a diagnosis on degradation. Proven end to end: a real broken canary, a real diagnosis, a real fix PR. The application chart is verified live the same day.', href: gh('airframe') },
  { date: '2026-08-12', title: 'Design resolved, build starts', text: 'The GitOps strategy and service-catalog design settle, and the platform around Glidepath begins: Crossplane as the control plane, ArgoCD for delivery, Backstage as the pane of glass.', href: gh('hangar', 'docs/gitops-strategy.md') },
];
---
<Base title="Log" description="Hangar's history: what changed, when, and why." section="log">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Log</p>
      <h1>Hangar is never finished</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Hangar is where I try things, so it keeps changing as I learn. These are the milestones so far, newest first,
        each linked to the place where I wrote down what happened and why.
      </p>
    </section>
    <ol class="log">
      {entries.map((e) => (
        <li>
          <time datetime={e.date}>{shortDate(e.date)}</time>
          <div>
            <h3>{e.href ? <a href={e.href}>{e.title}</a> : e.title}</h3>
            <p>{e.text}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .log { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .log li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7.5rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  time { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--accent); padding-top: 0.35rem; }
  .log h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .log h3 a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; }
  .log h3 a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .log p { margin: 0; max-width: var(--prose); color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .log li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.2rem; } }
</style>
